  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(10\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2x+3))=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2x+3):$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13996467/assets/bb49c052cabe12e8869270ab61b1de9e7f45b6acd6eaa9bc0d4c6892446a7cb6.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2x+3)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2x+3)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(10\\operatorname{arctan}\u2061(2x+3))=(10\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})=5\\pi .\n$$",
